defmodule InfluxElixir.Contract.SQLScalarRefusals do
  @moduledoc """
  The cases of the `*_refusable` tables that `Client.Local` refuses by name instead
  of answering, as `{kind, text, reason}`: the pin of the ratchet in
  `InfluxElixir.Contract.SQLScalar`.

  The pin is a set of cases, not a number of them. A case that is refused now and
  is not listed has regressed; a case that is listed and is answered now has been
  fixed, and moves out of its refusable table into the table of answers (and out of
  the list here). Swapping one for another fails twice, once for each, where a count
  would hold. A real engine refuses none of them.

  The `reason` is the exact text after `Client.Local: ` that the double gives. A case
  refused for another reason fails with both, so that a refusal cannot change what it
  says (or turn into a different refusal) unnoticed; when the wording of a reason is
  changed on purpose, its pins change with it.

  To list the cases of a table: run it against `Client.Local`, and keep the ones for
  which `InfluxElixir.Contract.SQLScalar.refusal_reason/1` of the answer is not `nil`,
  with that reason.
  """

  @doc "The cases refused of `expressions_values_refusable/0` of `SQLScalarCases`."
  @spec expressions_values() :: [{atom(), binary(), binary()}]
  def expressions_values do
    [
      {:sel, "s ~ 's[01]'",
       "unsupported column: s ~ 's[01]' as r (the character ~ is not one it reads)"},
      {:sel, "s !~ 's[01]'",
       "unsupported column: s !~ 's[01]' as r (the character ! is not one it reads)"},
      {:sel, "s ~* 'S1'",
       "unsupported column: s ~* 'S1' as r (the character ~ is not one it reads)"},
      {:raw, "SELECT u, CASE WHEN u > 3 THEN u ELSE 0 END AS a FROM mext ORDER BY time",
       "a CASE whose results are an unsigned integer beside another number: the engine's common type for them is not modelled"},
      {:raw, "SELECT u, pow(u, 2) AS a FROM mext ORDER BY time",
       "pow of an unsigned or narrow integer: the engine's coercion for it is not modelled"},
      {:sel, "greatest(time, time)",
       "greatest of arguments with no common type the double models"},
      {:sel, "coalesce(time, time)",
       "COALESCE of Timestamp(ns): they have no common type the double models (it models Int64, Float64, text and Boolean, each beside its own kind)"},
      {:sel, "nullif(time, time)",
       "NULLIF of Timestamp(ns): they have no common type the double models (it models Int64, Float64, text and Boolean, each beside its own kind)"},
